 The Android debug manifest permits that LAN HTTP workflow. Production builds reject cleartext traffic, so a signed/Play Store build must use an HTTPS API. Development and direct APK testing are free; Google Play developer registration is a separate store cost.
 
+## Production release gate
+
+The repository now fails closed for production configuration: `NODE_ENV=production` cannot run with demo mode, a missing database, a short/placeholder JWT secret, or an invalid port. The API exposes liveness/readiness endpoints, verifies the database before accepting production traffic, attaches request IDs, bounds in-memory rate-limit cleanup and shuts down HTTP, Socket.IO, Apollo and Prisma gracefully.
+
+Copy `.env.production.example` to your deployment secret manager/environment, replace every placeholder, then run:
+
+```bash
+npm run production:check
+```
+
+This check prints only integration booleans/status and never secret values. A real final release still requires external runtime proof for Firebase, PostgreSQL/Supabase Storage and any teacher-required Gemini response.
+
