+# Phase 10 — production hardening candidate
+
+Version: 0.9.2
+
+This phase moves EduPath BD from a QA-passed classroom build toward a fail-closed production release candidate without pretending that external cloud credentials have already been provisioned.
+
+## Code-level production work completed
+
+- Production mode refuses `DEMO_MODE=true`.
+- Non-demo mode refuses to start without `DATABASE_URL` and a strong JWT secret.
+- Placeholder JWT secrets are rejected in production.
+- A dedicated `npm run production:check` gate validates the required deployment configuration without printing secrets.
+- `/api/health/live` provides liveness and `/api/health/ready` verifies PostgreSQL readiness.
+- Production startup verifies database connectivity before the API begins listening.
+- Graceful SIGTERM/SIGINT shutdown closes Socket.IO, HTTP, Apollo and Prisma.
+- Every API response receives an `X-Request-Id`; unexpected errors return the request ID for support/debugging.
+- Rate-limit buckets are periodically pruned to prevent unbounded growth in a long-running single-node process.
+- Docker health checking uses the readiness endpoint and Docker no longer supplies an insecure fallback JWT secret.
+- Mobile E2E authentication follows the actual responsive breakpoint instead of racing visibility changes.
+- Android/iOS/repository release version advanced to 0.9.2 / build 20.
+- A dedicated signed-AAB release builder enforces HTTPS API targeting and external keystore credentials; signing secrets never belong in source control.
+
+## Still required before calling v1.0 production-complete
+
+1. Provision PostgreSQL/Supabase and run committed migrations + seed on the target environment.
+2. Configure Firebase project/Admin credentials and prove email/phone verification on a physical phone.
+3. Configure Supabase Storage and prove a real phone upload/preview.
+4. Configure an HTTPS production API URL and run the Android release build against it.
+5. Run `npm run production:check`, `npm run qa`, `npm run test:e2e` and `npm run audit:critical` with final environment/build inputs.
+6. Create/sign the Android AAB and complete final physical-phone acceptance.
+7. Obtain a green hosted GitHub Actions run.
+8. Produce the Windows Crystal Reports `.rpt` evidence if required by the course.
+9. Configure Gemini only if the teacher requires live generative-AI proof; the deterministic fallback remains honest and usable without a key.
+
+## Release rule
+
+Do not label the build `v1.0 production` until the runtime proof items above are complete. Version 0.9.2 is the production-hardened release candidate source.
